{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-008", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Equator Renewables Asia unveils 250 kW containerized PV system", "content": "<p>Singapore-based Equator Renewables Asia has developed a modular, relocatable PV system featuring up to 250 kW of solar capacity in a 40-foot shipping container. The plug-and-play solution uses n-type TOPCon bifacial modules and can be deployed by two workers in approximately two to three hours, according to the company.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/equator-renewables-asia-unveils-250-kw-containerized-pv-system/\">Equator Renewables Asia unveils 250 kW contain", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/equator-renewables-asia-unveils-250-kw-containerized-pv-system/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-009", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar sector corporate funding increases 45% through three quarters of 2026", "content": "<p>Total corporate funding into the solar sector, including venture capital, public market financing, and debt financing, reached $25.1 billion through three quarters of 2026, according to a report from Mercom Capital Group.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/solar-sector-corporate-funding-increases-45-through-three-quarters-of-2026/\">Solar sector corporate funding increases 45% through three quarters of 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/solar-sector-corporate-funding-increases-45-through-three-quarters-of-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-010", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Armenia introduces interest rate subsidies for storage systems", "content": "<p>New government provisions offer businesses interest rate subsidies of 6 to 10 percentage points on loans and leases for battery storage equipment.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/armenia-introduces-interest-rate-subsidies-for-storage-systems/\">Armenia introduces interest rate subsidies for storage systems</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/armenia-introduces-interest-rate-subsidies-for-storage-systems/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-011", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The impact of dust and shading on pole-mounted PV", "content": "<p>A year-long comparison of five PV configurations highlights how maintenance access, shading, and structural limits influence off-grid system selection. The researchers combined field measurements with analytical models to quantify these constraints and guide configuration choices.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/the-impact-of-dust-and-shading-on-pole-mounted-pv/\">The impact of dust and shading on pole-mounted PV</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/the-impact-of-dust-and-shading-on-pole-mounted-pv/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-012", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Japan proposes 50-metric-ton trigger for solar panel recycling plans", "content": "<p>A Japanese government study group is weighing rules that would bring almost all conventional solar panels under a new recycling law, while leaving perovskite and flexible modules out for now.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/japan-proposes-50-metric-ton-trigger-for-solar-panel-recycling-plans/\">Japan proposes 50-metric-ton trigger for solar panel recycling plans</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/japan-proposes-50-metric-ton-trigger-for-solar-panel-recycling-plans/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-013", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Belgian spin-off Noak raises €5 million for perovskite-silicon solar cells", "content": "<p>Noak will use the seed funding to industrialise its perovskite-silicon tandem technology, which combines a proprietary layer stack with a 3D woven back-contact foil.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/belgian-spin-off-noak-raises-e5-million-for-perovskite-silicon-solar-cells/\">Belgian spin-off Noak raises €5 million for perovskite-silicon solar cells</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/belgian-spin-off-noak-raises-e5-million-for-perovskite-silicon-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-014", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Zwitterions could be much more than defect passivators in perovskite solar cells", "content": "<p>Chinese researchers have reviewed the potential of zwitterions to improve the efficiency and stability of perovskite solar cells through defect passivation, crystallization control, and interface engineering. They found that these compounds could also enhance charge extraction, stabilize the perovskite structure, and suppress ion migration and electrode degradation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/zwitterions-could-be-much-more-than-defect-passivators-in-perovs", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/zwitterions-could-be-much-more-than-defect-passivators-in-perovskite-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-015", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Pakistan seeks consultant for distributed solar project", "content": "<p>A tender is open in Pakistan searching for a consultant to verify all non-solar works that form part of a 100 MW distributed PV project in the region of Gilgit-Baltistan. The deadline for expressions of interest is November 30.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/pakistan-seeks-consultant-for-distributed-solar-project/\">Pakistan seeks consultant for distributed solar project</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/pakistan-seeks-consultant-for-distributed-solar-project/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-02-016", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Retractable photovoltaics for wastewater treatment", "content": "<p>Germany’s largest retractable solar roof, with a capacity of 2.745 MW, is under construction at a wastewater treatment plant in Stuttgart. Scheduled for completion in 2027, the system will generate more than 2.2 GWh annually, covering around 9% of the plant’s electricity demand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/retractable-photovoltaics-for-wastewater-treatment/\">Retractable photovoltaics for wastewater treatment</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/02/retractable-photovoltaics-for-wastewater-treatment/", "type": "rss"}]}
